  "_comment": "REGGAE drum patterns (drum-role space). Encoded from the drum grids in docs/idiom-research/genre-reggae-dub-bass.md sections A6/A8 and B6. Rhythm archetypes are unprotectable scenes a faire (docs/idiom-research/legal.md), so the canonical named patterns are encoded as-is: the one-drop, rockers, steppers, the flying-cymbal hat. Grid law at the pack's 66-92 BPM one-drop feel: skank lands on b=1.0 and b=3.0 (beats 2 and 4), so the one-drop kick+side-stick sit at b=2.0 (beat 3) and beat 1 is LEFT OPEN (corny trap A8.1: a kick on beat 1 kills the one-drop). Side-stick (rim) carries the backbeat; the full snare is reserved for fills and the dub snare bomb (A8.6). Engine applies the pack swing.",
